cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ArchytasZX: Size- and Dimension-Agnostic Engine for Quantum Algorithm Development Based on ZX-Calculus"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dmitriev
    given-names: Arkhip Alekseyevich
repository-code: "https://github.com/Arhip-Dmitriev/ArchytasZX"
url: "https://github.com/Arhip-Dmitriev/ArchytasZX"
abstract: >-
  A symbolic engine for developing quantum algorithms without fixing the qudit
  count or dimension, built on the qufinite ZX(W)-calculus with its own Dirac
  notation language. States, Born distributions and proofs are derived as closed
  forms by exact rewriting, never by simulation. Includes bang boxes and scalable
  notation, a normal-form procedure, equality saturation, proof search,
  induction over symbolic multiplicities, replayable certificates, a proof
  kernel, and export of proofs and refutations to Lean 4 and Mathlib.
keywords:
  - zx-calculus
  - qufinite
  - qudit
  - quantum computing
  - symbolic algebra
  - graph rewriting
  - quantum algorithms
  - symbolic quantum
  - graphical calculus
  - dirac notation
  - formal verification
  - lean
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-23"
